#+TITLE: fehqlibs-dev — DSMR Package Documentation
#+AUTHOR: Brian O'Reilly <fade@deepsky.com>
#+DATE: 2026-03-22

* Summary

~fehqlibs-dev~ packages the fehQlibs static library collection (release 30) by
Erwin Hoffman.  fehQlibs provides the low-level network, DNS, string, buffer,
and socket primitives that ucspi-ssl depends on at build time.  The package
installs to ~/usr/lib/fehqlibs/~, satisfying Debian Policy §9.1.2 by keeping
all files under ~/usr~.

| Field       | Value                              |
|-------------+------------------------------------|
| Source      | fehqlibs                           |
| Binary      | fehqlibs-dev                       |
| Version     | 30-1                               |
| Architecture| any                                |
| Install to  | ~/usr/lib/fehqlibs/~               |
| Target      | Debian 13 Trixie                   |

* Description

fehQlibs is a djbware-derived utility library maintained by Erwin Hoffman at
fehcom.de.  It bundles two static archives:

- ~libqlibs.a~ (~qlibs.a~) — buffer, string, socket, byte, and general
  utility routines used throughout the djb tool chain.
- ~libdnsresolv.a~ (~dnsresolv.a~) — asynchronous, DNSSEC-aware DNS
  resolution routines required by ucspi-ssl for certificate hostname
  verification.

The package builds these libraries from source and installs them to
~/usr/lib/fehqlibs/~, with both the canonical ~libXXX.a~ names and the
legacy ~XXX.a~ names (as symlinks) so that upstream build systems that
reference either naming convention work without patching.

Headers are installed to ~/usr/lib/fehqlibs/include/~.  Downstream packages
point their ~conf-qlibs~ (or equivalent) at ~/usr/lib/fehqlibs~ at build time.
There is no runtime component; this is a build-time dependency only.

** Why not /usr/local?

Earlier revisions installed to ~/usr/local/qlibs/~, which dpkg rejects under
Policy §9.1.2 (~/usr/local~ is reserved for the local administrator).  Moving
to ~/usr/lib/fehqlibs/~ fixes the lintian ~E: dir-in-usr-local~ violation and
makes the path stable for downstream packages.

* TL;DR Runtime Documentation

fehqlibs is a *build-time-only* package.  Once installed there is nothing to
run, configure, or administer.

** Installing

#+BEGIN_SRC sh
sudo dpkg -i fehqlibs-dev_30-1_amd64.deb
#+END_SRC

Verify the installation:

#+BEGIN_SRC sh
ls /usr/lib/fehqlibs/
# libqlibs.a  qlibs.a  libdnsresolv.a  dnsresolv.a  include/
#+END_SRC

** Building dependent packages

Packages that use fehqlibs (e.g. ucspi-ssl) must point their ~conf-qlibs~
file at ~/usr/lib/fehqlibs~ before running ~make~.  The ucspi-ssl package
does this automatically via the ~debian-install-paths.patch~ quilt patch.

** Rebuilding from source

#+BEGIN_SRC sh
cd fehQlibs-30
dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
#+END_SRC
